** Both materials share one elastic-plastic law, so the WHOLE bar
** yields together and contracts laterally without mismatch.  That
** keeps the stress field uniformly uniaxial, which linear tetrahedra
** represent exactly, so the 1-D reference above is the FE answer and
** not just an estimate.  A single plastic slice between elastic
** blocks would instead be laterally constrained and would carry an
** axial stress well above sigma_y.
** The slices differ ONLY in that the weak one can damage.
